Kernir patch 0007: a data CRC mismatch fails the entry in the 7zip and LHA readers

Upstream: libarchive 3.8.10, libarchive/archive_read_support_format_7zip.c
(archive_read_format_7zip_read_data) and libarchive/archive_read_support_format_lha.c
(lha_end_of_entry).

Upstream reports a file whose data does not match its stored CRC only as ARCHIVE_WARN ("7-Zip bad
CRC: 0x.. should be 0x..", "LHa data CRC error"; the LHA one arrives in place of the end of the data),
so a caller that accepts warnings extracts damaged bytes without an error and a repack launders them
with a fresh CRC. Both are now ARCHIVE_FAILED with the same message, as the zip, rar, rar5 and cab
readers already do. On 7zip this extends patch 0004, which made the mismatch ARCHIVE_FAILED in an
encrypted folder only. Under DONT_FAIL_ON_CRC_ERROR the upstream (and 0004) behaviour is kept.

Apply from Sources/CLibArchive: patch -p1 < patches/0007-7zip-lha-data-crc-fails.patch

--- a/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_7zip.c
+++ b/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_7zip.c
@@ -1226,8 +1226,14 @@
 			    (unsigned long)zip->si.ss.digests[
 			    		zip->entry->ssIndex]);
 			/* Kernir patch 0004: in an encrypted folder this is
-			 * what a wrong passphrase looks like; never a warning. */
+			 * what a wrong passphrase looks like; never a warning.
+			 * Kernir patch 0007: nor in a plain folder, where it is
+			 * damaged data. */
+#ifndef DONT_FAIL_ON_CRC_ERROR
+			ret = ARCHIVE_FAILED;
+#else
 			ret = zip->aes_folder ? ARCHIVE_FAILED : ARCHIVE_WARN;
+#endif
 		}
 	}
 
--- a/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_lha.c
+++ b/libarchive/archive_read_support_format_lha.c
@@ -1469,7 +1469,12 @@
 		    lha->crc != lha->entry_crc_calculated) {
 			archive_set_error(&a->archive, ARCHIVE_ERRNO_MISC,
 			    "LHa data CRC error");
+			/* Kernir patch 0007: damaged data fails the entry. */
+#ifndef DONT_FAIL_ON_CRC_ERROR
+			r = ARCHIVE_FAILED;
+#else
 			r = ARCHIVE_WARN;
+#endif
 		}
 
 		/* End-of-entry cleanup done. */
